WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:00.880
You fixed

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.080
a checkout button,

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:02.480
but you

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:02.960
also have

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.800
an unfinished experiment.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.920
Your next commit

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:06.560
should tell

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.000
one clear story.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:08.760
Git add

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:09.520
lets you

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.720
choose which changes

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:11.640
belong in it.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.800
Adding stages the

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.080
chosen file content

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.280
in the index,

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:16.920
also called

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.280
the staging area.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:18.600
Pick the

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.720
button fix and

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:20.840
leave the experiment

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.560
outside.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:22.040
You can

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.320
even choose selected

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.360
changes within one

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:24.960
file.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:26.400
Here is

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:26.800
the detail

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.520
that matters.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:28.560
Git stages the

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.120
content as

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:29.440
it is

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:29.760
when you

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.280
add it.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:30.640
If you

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.280
edit that

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.400
same file again,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.440
stage those later

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.160
edits again

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:34.480
if you

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.400
want them included.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.040
Adding prepares your next

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:38.600
commit.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.080
It does

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:39.720
not record

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.760
that commit or

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.120
upload anything.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:42.600
Think of

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.000
it as

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.120
choosing what goes

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:44.600
into the

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.880
next package before

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:46.800
you seal it.
